	<div id="divFaqsPopup">
		<div class="divPopupHeading">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
		<div id="btnCloseFaqs"></div>
		<div id="divFaqsList">
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>1. General Questions</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What is the Sport Predictor?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">The Sport Predictor is a free-to-play prediction competition where you predict the outcome of tournament matches before kick-off.<br/>Depending on the tournament, you either predict the exact final score (<span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode</span>) or predict which team will win and by how many points (<span class="textPurple">Win By mode</span>).<br/>You earn points for correct scores and correct results, climb leaderboards, compete in pools, and stand a chance to win prizes throughout the tournament.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Which sports are supported?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">The Sport Predictor supports multiple divisions of rugby and soccer.<br/>Each tournament may have its own scoring configuration, rules, and prizes. Check the tournament's "How It Works" section for individual tournament details.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Is it free to participate?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. The Sport Predictor is completely free to participate in.<br/>You do not need to pay an entry fee to make predictions, join the Global Pool, compete on leaderboards, or take part in the competition.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Who can enter?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Anyone who is 18 years or older and has a play.co.za account.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do the Terms and Conditions apply?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. These FAQs are a simple guide to help users understand how the competition works.<br/>The official Terms and Conditions apply to all entries, prizes, Free Bets, leaderboards, tie-breakers, wagering requirements, verification, and eligibility.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What do I need to do?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">You need to make a prediction for each match before kick-off. The prediction format depends on the tournament mode:<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode</span>: Predict each team's final score (e.g. Team A 22 - Team B 17).<br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode:</span> Predict which team wins and by how many points (e.g. Team A by 5, or Draw).<br/><br/>If your prediction matches the actual result exactly, you earn maximum points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do I need to predict every match?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. You do not need to predict every match to appear on the leaderboards.<br/>However, the more matches you predict, the more chances you have to earn points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I skip matches?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You can skip matches, but you will receive 0 points for any match where you do not submit a prediction.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I have more than one account?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. Users are not allowed to create or use multiple accounts.<br/>Each user may only participate with one account. Multiple accounts may result in disqualification and prize forfeiture.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>2. How Points Work</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do I earn points?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">You earn points based on how accurate your prediction is. Each tournament may award different point values, but the categories are:<br/><br/>Correct Score (CS) - Your prediction matched exactly. In <span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode</span> this means both teams' scores are correct. In <span class="textPurple">Win By mode</span> this means the correct winner and exact margin.<br/>Correct Result (CR) - You predicted the correct outcome (win/loss/draw) but not the exact score or margin.<br/>Margin Points (MP) - Awarded when your prediction is close to the actual result (within the margin grace).<br/>Incorrect Result - 0 points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What is a Correct Score?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">A Correct Score means your prediction matched the actual result exactly.<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode:</span><br/>You predict 22-17. The match ends 22-17. You earn Correct Score points.<br/><br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode:</span><br/>You predict Team A by 5. Team A wins by exactly 5 points. You earn Correct Score points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What is a Correct Result?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">A Correct Result means you predicted the correct match outcome (which team wins, or a draw) but not the exact score or margin.<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode:</span><br/>You predict 22-17 (Team A wins). The match ends 15-10 (Team A wins). You picked the correct winning team, so you earn Correct Result points.<br/><br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode:</span><br/>You predict Team A by 10. Team A wins by 3. You picked the correct winning team but not the exact margin, so you earn Correct Result points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What are Margin Points?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Margin Points reward predictions that are close to the actual result, even if they are not exact.<br/><br/>Each tournament has a Margin Grace value. If the difference between your prediction and the actual result falls within the margin grace, you earn Margin Points.<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode</span> (margin grace of 7):<br/>You predict 24-17. The match ends 22-14. The differences are 2 (home) and 3 (away), totalling 5. Since 5 is within the margin grace of 7, you earn Margin Points.<br/><br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode</span> (margin grace of 7):<br/>You predict Team A by 10. Team A wins by 5. The difference is 5. Since 5 is within the margin grace of 7, you earn Margin Points.<br/><br/>Note: Margin Points are not available in every tournament. If disabled for a tournament, they will not appear on the leaderboard.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What is an incorrect result?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">An incorrect result means your predicted outcome did not match the actual result.<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode:</span><br/>You predict Team A to win (e.g. 22-17), but Team B wins or the match ends in a draw. You earn 0 points.<br/><br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode:</span><br/>You predict Team A to win, but Team B wins or the match ends in a draw. You earn 0 points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How are draw predictions scored?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">If you predict a draw and the match ends in a draw, you can earn points.<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode:</span><br/>You predict 15-15. The match ends 15-15. You earn Correct Score points.<br/>You predict 15-15 and the match ends 12-12. You earn Correct Result points because you correctly predicted a draw.<br/><br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode:</span><br/>You predict Draw. The match ends in a draw. You earn Correct Score points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I earn points if I get the winner right but the score wrong?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You will earn Correct Result points. You may also earn Margin Points if the tournament supports them and your prediction is close enough to the actual score.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I earn points if I get the scores right but the result wrong?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. If the winning team is wrong, you earn 0 points regardless of the prediction mode.<br/><br/><span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode:</span><br/>You predict 22-17, but the match ends 17-22. The scores are swapped, meaning the winning team is wrong, so you earn 0 points.<br/><br/><span class="textPurple">Win By mode:</span><br/>You predict Team A by 5, but Team B wins. The winning team is wrong, so you earn 0 points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What do CR, CS, MP, TMD, and TP mean on the leaderboard?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">CR = Correct Results - the number of times you predicted the correct outcome.<br/>CS = Correct Scores - the number of times your prediction matched exactly.<br/>MP = Margin Points - bonus points for predictions close to the actual result.<br/>TMD = Total Margin Difference - the combined difference between your predictions and the actual results across all matches.<br/>TP = Total Points - your total score on the leaderboard.<br/><br/>Note: MP and TMD columns may be hidden if the tournament does not use Margin Points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do point values change between tournaments?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. Each tournament may have its own point values for Correct Score, Correct Result, Margin Points, and Margin Grace.<br/>The point values for the current tournament are displayed in the tournament details.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>3. Making Predictions</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do I make a prediction?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Click Make Your Picks.<br/>If the tournament has multiple rounds, you can select which round to predict. Then enter your predictions for the available matches.<br/><br/>In <span class="textBlue">Exact Score mode</span> you will see two pickers per match to set each team's score. In <span class="textPurple">Win By mode</span> you will see a single picker to select the winner and margin.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">When must I submit my prediction?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Predictions must be submitted before the match kicks off.<br/>Once the match has started, predictions for that match will close.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I change my prediction after submitting it?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">You can change your prediction before kick-off, as long as the prediction window for that match is still open.<br/>Once the match has started, your prediction is locked and cannot be changed.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What happens if I forget to submit a prediction?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">You will receive 0 points for that match.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Will I get a reminder before matches start?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Where available, the platform may send reminders before selected matches, but it remains your responsibility to submit predictions before kick-off.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I see other users' predictions?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. You will only be able to see your own picks.<br/>Other users' predictions will not be visible unless play.co.za decides to share them after the leaderboard has been concluded.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>4. Match Result Rules</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Which score counts for predictions?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Only the official match result at the end of regulation time will count for prediction purposes.<br/>For rugby, this is the score after 80 minutes including stoppage or injury time.<br/>For soccer, this is the score after 90 minutes including stoppage or injury time.<br/>Extra time and penalty shootouts do not count.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do penalty shootouts or extra time count?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. Penalty shootouts and extra time do not count.<br/>Only the regulation-time result will be used for prediction scoring.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What happens if a match is postponed?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">If a match is postponed, predictions may remain valid for the rescheduled match.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What happens if a match is cancelled or abandoned?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">If a match is cancelled and not replayed, the match may be voided for prediction and leaderboard purposes.<br/>If a match is abandoned, the result will be handled according to the verified official match outcome used by the platform.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What happens if the official result changes later?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">If the official result is corrected or updated after the match, leaderboard points may be updated according to the verified result used by the platform.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>5. How Pools Work</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What are Pools?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Pools are a way to compete against friends, family, colleagues, or your own group.<br/>You can compete inside your pool while still being part of the Global Pool.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Am I automatically added to the Global Pool?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. Anyone who saves a pick is automatically added to the Global Pool for that tournament.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What about Round Pools?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Some tournaments have separate leaderboards for each round consisting of 1 or more matches per round. If a tournament has round pools, you are automatically added when you submit picks for matches in that round.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I be in multiple pools at the same time?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You can be in the Global Pool, round pools, and your own custom pools simultaneously.<br/>Your pool lets you compare yourself against your friends, while the Global Pool shows where you rank against everyone.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do I create a pool?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Go to Leaderboards and select Create Pool.<br/><br/>You will need to set:<br/>A pool name and optionally a password.<br/>You can then share the pool name and password with your friends so they can join.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do my friends join my pool?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Your friends must go to Join Pool and search for your pool name.<br/>Once they find it, they will enter the password (if set) and join the pool.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do my picks change between pools?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. Your saved picks apply to the entire tournament.<br/>Your points reflect across all pools and leaderboards you are part of.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>6. Leaderboards & Prizes</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do leaderboards work?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Leaderboards rank all participants by their total points. The Global Pool leaderboard covers the entire tournament.<br/>If the tournament has multiple rounds, there may also be separate round leaderboards where you compete for that round's prizes.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do I improve my leaderboard ranking?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Submit predictions for as many matches as possible and aim for exact predictions.<br/>Correct scores earn the most points. If the tournament uses Margin Points, getting close to the actual result also helps.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Are there prizes for round leaderboards?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Some tournaments offer prizes for each round leaderboard. Where round prizes are available, they will be displayed on the platform.<br/>Not all tournaments have round prizes. Smaller tournaments may only have an overall prize pool.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I win more than one prize?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You can win prizes across different rounds and on the overall leaderboard.<br/>However, you are not allowed to use multiple accounts.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">When are leaderboard winners decided?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Winners are decided after all matches in the relevant round or tournament have been completed and the leaderboard has been concluded.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>7. Prize Terms & Wagering</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do I need to deposit to play?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. The Sport Predictor is free to play. You do not need to deposit to make predictions or compete on leaderboards.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do cash prizes have wagering requirements?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">If you have deposited at least R100 in total, you will have 0x wagering on your cash prizes.<br/>If you have deposited less than R100, your cash prize will be subject to a 20x wagering requirement.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What does 20x wagering mean?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">A 20x wagering requirement means you must wager the prize amount 20 times before the prize or eligible winnings can be withdrawn.<br/><br/>Example:<br/>You win a R1 000 cash prize and have not deposited R100.<br/>R1 000 x 20 = R20 000.<br/>You must wager R20 000 before the prize or eligible winnings can be withdrawn.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What counts as a lifetime deposit?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Successful real-money deposits made into your play.co.za account.<br/>Bonus funds, Free Bets, promotional credits, cancelled deposits, reversed deposits, or refunded deposits do not count toward the R100 minimum.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do I need to be verified before receiving a prize?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You need to be fully verified through KYC/FICA before receiving any prize.<br/>If you cannot complete the required verification, you may not be able to receive your prize.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">When are prizes paid?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Prizes will be paid within 30 days after the relevant leaderboard has been concluded, but payment will be made as soon as possible.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>8. Free Bets</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What is a Free Bet?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">A Free Bet is a promotional betting credit that may be awarded as a prize.<br/>Different Free Bets may have different rules, so you should always read the Free Bet terms before using it.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How does a Free Bet work?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">A Free Bet must be used to place a bet.<br/>Some Free Bets may require minimum odds before they can be used.<br/><br/>Example:<br/>You receive a R100 Free Bet. You place it on a selection with odds of 2.00. If the bet wins, the total return is R200.<br/>However, you only keep the winnings. The original R100 Free Bet stake is not returned.<br/>In this example, your cashable winning amount would be R100, not R200.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do I keep the Free Bet stake if I win?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. You only keep the winnings from the Free Bet.<br/>The original Free Bet amount is not returned.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can a Free Bet be withdrawn as cash?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">No. A Free Bet cannot be withdrawn as cash.<br/>Only qualifying winnings from a successful Free Bet may be withdrawable, depending on the Free Bet rules.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>9. Tie-Breakers</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Why are tie-breakers needed?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Tie-breakers are used when two or more players finish with the same number of total points on a leaderboard.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How are ties resolved?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">The following tie-breaker order is used:<br/><br/>1. Total Points (highest first)<br/>2. Total Margin Difference (lowest first, meaning closer predictions rank higher)<br/>3. Most Correct Scores<br/>4. Earliest participation (first to join ranks higher)<br/><br/>If a tournament does not use Margin Points, the Total Margin Difference step is skipped.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">If I tie for a prize, do I share it?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">If a shared prize rule applies, tied users may share the prize.<br/>If tie-breakers apply, the final positions will be decided using the tie-breaker rules above.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>10. My Progress</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What is My Progress?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">My Progress is your personal dashboard for tracking your prediction performance throughout the tournament.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">What can I see in My Progress?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Your My Progress page shows:<br/>Total points, Correct scores, Correct results, Current round ranking (if applicable), and Overall ranking.<br/>If the tournament has a Grand Prize, you will also see your progress toward the required number of correct scores.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How often is My Progress updated?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">My Progress updates after match results have been confirmed and points have been calculated.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Why did my ranking change?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Your ranking can change as more match results are confirmed and other users earn points.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can my points change after they are awarded?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. Points may change if an official result is corrected or if there is a scoring adjustment.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="divFaqItem">
				<div class="divFaqButton">
					<span>11. Prize Payments & Verification</span>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">How do I know if I have won a prize?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Winners will appear on the relevant leaderboard once the leaderboard has been concluded.<br/>Some prizes may be claimed directly through the app, while others may be allocated manually. Prize winners may also be contacted through their registered contact details.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Do I need to verify my account to receive a prize?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You need to be fully verified through KYC/FICA before receiving a prize.<br/>If you cannot complete the required verification, you may not be able to receive your prize.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">When are prizes paid?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Prizes will be paid within 30 days after the relevant leaderboard has been concluded, but payment will be made as soon as possible.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="divFaqContent">
					<div class="divFaqQuestion">Can I win more than one prize?</div>
					<div class="divFaqAnswer">Yes. You can win prizes across different rounds and on the overall leaderboard.<br/>However, you are not allowed to use multiple accounts.</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
